#include \(dqbashclient.h\(dq

typedef void (*bc_pty_output_cb)(const char *data, size_t len,
                                 void *userdata);

void bc_pty_on_output(bc_client_t *c, bc_pty_output_cb cb,
                      void *userdata);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Registers a callback function that is invoked whenever output data
arrives from the active PTY session.
The callback receives decoded output bytes from the PTY child process.
.PP
The \f[B]data\f[R] passed to the callback is raw terminal output.
If ANSI stripping was enabled in \f[CR]bc_pty_spawn(3)\f[R], the data
has already been filtered by the server\-side \f[CR]ansi_strip(3)\f[R]
function and contains no escape sequences.
Otherwise, it may contain ANSI escape sequences, control characters, and
arbitrary binary data.
.PP
\f[B]The callback is only invoked during \f[CB]bc_poll(3)\f[B]
calls.\f[R] The client must call \f[CR]bc_poll\f[R] regularly (in an
event loop or polling cycle) for output to be delivered.
.PP
To unregister the callback, call
\f[CR]bc_pty_on_output(c, NULL, NULL)\f[R].
.SH Wire protocol
Output arrives on \f[CR]CHAN_PTY\f[R] (channel 5) as:
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq:\(dqoutput\(dq,\(dqdata\(dq:\(dqbHMgLWxhCg==\(dq}
.EE
.PP
The \f[CR]data\f[R] field is base64\-encoded.
The library decodes it before invoking the callback.
